    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265-a1">

                <pb facs="0446" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg350"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Belknap to Mr. Fish.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War
                                Department</hi>. <hi rendition="#italic">Washington
                            City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-11-04"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">November</hi> 4, 1871</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 31st ultimo, inclosing copy of a dispatch from the
                    commercial agent of the United States at Guerrero, Mexico, in relation to an
                    attack of Indians from that part of Mexico, on the adjacent settlements in
                    Texas.</p>
                <p>In connection therewith I have the honor to invite your attention to the
                    accompanying copy of remarks of the General of the Army, to whom your letter was
                    referred for his views.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. W. BELKNAP,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        War.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
